## Ignore Visual Studio temporary files, build results, and
## files generated by popular Visual Studio add-ons.

## User-specific files
*.rsuser
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.userprefs

## Visual Studio cache/options folders
.vs/
.vscode/

## Build results
bin/
obj/
[Bb]uild/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/

## Publish output
publish/
*.Publish.xml
*.deploy
*.deployment

## NuGet packages
*.nupkg
packages/
# For PackageReference-based projects:
# project.lock.json
project.assets.json
.nuget/

## Rider & ReSharper
_ReSharper*/
*.DotSettings.user
.idea/

## Log, temporary, database files
*.log
*.tlog
*.tmp
*.temp
*.cache
*.bak
*.backup
*.dbmdl
*.sqlite
*.mdf
*.ldf
*.ndf

## VS Code specific
.vscode/

## DotCover / Test Results
*.dotCover
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coveragexml

## Others
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.pdb
*.sdf
*.opensdf
*.unsuccessfulbuild